\par\par \b \uc2  UPDATE 2- \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia \highlight\uc2  c.bank  \highlight22\uc2 intervening \highlight\uc2  to prop up rupiah. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Joanne Collins and Harry Suhartono \par \uc2 405 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Juli 2003\par 08:08\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, July 23 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  scrambled to put a floor under the shaky rupiah \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday after it hit an 11-week low against the dollar, but said it still had room to cautiously lower interest rates. \par \par \uc2  When asked if the bank was \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 , senior deputy governor Anwar Nasution told Reuters: "I cannot say exactly when or how much but I can assure you we are in the market." \par \par \uc2  He earlier told reporters that the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market should determine the rate of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and that there was little point to continuous \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  - a comment which helped drag the unit down. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah fell to 8,640 in morning deals, its lowest since May 5, but later recovered and at 0510 GMT was being quoted at 8,495/8,515. \par \par \uc2  Separately, the bank's governor, Burhanuddin Abdullah, told Reuters that the rupiah's fall was temporary and that interest rates could still head lower despite the rupiah's fall. \par \par \uc2  The weaker rupiah has raised concern over how much more inflation would ease in Indonesia, which still has one of the highest rates in Asia, and whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would have to curtail its policy of gradually lowering interest rates. \par \par \uc2  "We think it is something temporary. We will guard the rupiah exchange rate in the market so the movement will not disturb the economy," Abdullah said, adding \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was one option. \par \par \uc2  "Generally the policy will remain that there is still room to lower interest rates," he said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , under pressure since late last week, has been relatively stable and strong in recent months mainly due to short-term capital inflows. \par \par \uc2  Asked why the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had depreciated so rapidly, Nasution said: "Some companies saw the appreciation of the rupiah as an opportunity to re-pay their debts so they started buying U.S. dollars." \par \par \uc2  "The other reason might be demand from PLN and Pertamina," he said, referring to the state electricity utility and the national oil company, respectively. \par \par \uc2  Even at the current rates, the rupiah is stronger than the 9,000 average exchange rate assumed under the 2003 state budget. \par \par \uc2  In an interview with Reuters earlier this month, Nasution estimated the rupiah could strengthen to 8,000 per dollar in the third quarter but cautioned that those short-term inflows could also destabilise it. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030723dz7n0060p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
