\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -C.banks active as rupiah, baht, peso dip. \b0\par\par\uc2 780 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Juli 2003\par 11:04\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Vidya Ranganathan\par     SINGAPORE, July 23 (Reuters) - Policy-driven moves\par dominated Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  trade on Wednesday as the Indonesian\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  worked to rein in a tumbling rupiah, Korean\par authorities tried to talk down the won, and Thailand relaxed\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rules.\par     The Philippine peso weakened to four-month lows amid stray\par market rumours the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was also a buyer of dollars to\par meet heavy overseas bond repayment obligations in coming\par months.\par     "It seems as if everybody is just blatantly trying to\par manipulate their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  a little bit and fight this," said\par Claudio Piron, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist with Standard Chartered\par Bank, referring to China's yuan and the persistent contention\par by trading partners that it is undervalued.\par  \par     "And the other way to get around that problem is to\par liberalise as well," he said.\par     The Indonesian rupiah        lost almost two percent on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  Wednesday as it fell to 11-week lows of 8,640, with suspected \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  unable to counter the pressure from \par \par \uc2  foreign investors withdrawing their funds. \par \par \uc2  A top Korean finance ministry official said the won's \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par              strength was not justified, given the weak\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par economy, but it still closed local trade slightly stronger.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Thai baht  weakened past 42 per dollar after the\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  increased the amount that domestic investors could\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par hold in foreign bonds and extended the period exporters could\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par hold non-baht revenues in their foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  accounts.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Traders said the baht fell sharply but profit-taking\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par emerged at the 42.01 baht low, the weakest since the end of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par June.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Singapore dollar  was higher and the Taiwan\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar  was range-bound as traders watched funds move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par out of high-yielding \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  into growth plays, which are\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par expected to favour leveraged economies such as Singapore and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Taiwan.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Meanwhile, Philippine \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Deputy Governor Amando\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Tetangco tried to allay worries about the peso's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par weakness as it slipped to a four-month low of 54.055.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The peso movement is due mainly to expectation of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par month-end demand and weaker regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . This is the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par import season," he said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par RUPIAH TAKES A KNOCK\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Indonesian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  officials hastened to defend the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par falling rupiah as it sank to its lowest low since May 5 on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Wednesday - the second anniversary of Megawati Sukarnoputri's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par taking over as Indonesia's President.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Senior Deputy Governor Anwar Nasution initially said the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par market could determine the rupiah's level and there was no need\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  continuously, but later confirmed the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par had \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . Traders said Bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had been active on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par both Tuesday and Wednesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The bank's governor, Burhanuddin Abdullah, said the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rupiah's fall was temporary and interest rates still could head\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par lower.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The rupiah's slide had probably been triggered by the news\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par that BP Plc (BP.L) and global mining giant Rio Tinto (RIO.L)\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  (RIO.AX) were selling their Indonesian coal mine joint venture\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to a local firm for $500 million, traders said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But indications that foreign investment was leaving the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par country at the time when interest rates are falling and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par investors flocking to the more technology-dominated stock\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par markets in the region were worrisome, analysts said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     "There are so many smoking guns here," Piron said,\par referring to the potential risks for the rupiah.\par     JP Morgan analyst James Malcolm said Jakarta's markets had\par been complacent about the local risks of political stability\par and success in sales of bad loans during the past 18 months.\par     Slowing growth, the possibility reforms will be put on the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par backburner ahead of elections in 2004, and the uncertainty over\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par financing as the country opts out of a IMF loan programme could\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par all weigh on the rupiah, he said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par He revised his end-September rupiah forecast down to 9,000\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par per dollar from 7,500 per dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR AT 0817 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen     118.82       119.02         +0.17\par  Sing dlr      1.7562       1.7581         +0.11\par  Taiwan dlr    34.417       34.440         +0.07\par  Korean won   1182.80      1182.80          0.00\par  Baht           41.99        41.82         -0.40\par  Peso           54.03        53.85         -0.32\par  Rupiah       8550.00      8400.00         -1.75\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     118.82       118.74         -0.07\par  Sing dlr      1.7562       1.7341         -1.26\par  Taiwan dlr    34.417       34.753         +0.98\par  Korean won   1182.80      1185.80         +0.25\par  Baht           41.99        43.08         +2.60\par  Peso           54.03        53.38         -1.19\par  Rupiah       8550.00      8940.00         +4.56.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030723dz7n00iog\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pic