\par\par \b \uc2  Bk  \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia \highlight\uc2  Deputy Gov: Won't  \highlight22\uc2 Intervene \highlight\uc2  To Help Rupiah \b0\par\par\uc2 205 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Juli 2003\par 04:09\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2003, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA -(Dow Jones)- Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  won't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the rupiah, which fell to a fresh three-month low Wednesday as foreign investors took profit on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and local bonds, Senior Deputy Governor Anwar Nasution said. \par \par \uc2  "I don't think so," he said, when asked if the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. "We adopt a floating exchange rate policy and let the market decide." \par \par \uc2  His remarks contradict earlier comments by dealers, who suspect Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market since Monday to slow down the dollar's rise. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah fell to IDR8,540 to the dollar early Wednesday from its close Tuesday at IDR8,425 as foreign investors continued to take profit on the Indonesian unit and rupiah-denominated assets in the run-up to the annual session of the nation's highest legislative body, the MPR, early next month. \par \par \uc2  Although the session is expected to be peaceful, political temperatures are expected to rise, providing an excuse for market players to sell the rupiah and buy back the dollar. \par \par \uc2  -By Farida Husna, Dow Jones Newswires; 62-21 39831277; djn.jakarta@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  -Edited by Kevin Lim \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020030723dz7n0003w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\png