\par\par \b \uc2  Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Mixed On Equity Flows, \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Fear \b0\par\par\uc2 881 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Juni 2003\par 11:50\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2003, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  put up a mixed showing Thursday supported by strong equity inflows, but with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  theme a strong deterrent to attempts to take the units too high. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar, the Philippine peso and the Indonesian rupiah slipped, while the South Korean won, the Thai baht and the New Taiwan dollar were modestly higher. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said central banks in the region are loathe to allow their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to appreciate too fast for fear of losing export competitiveness at a time of uncertainty for the global economy. \par \par \uc2  "Across the board, central banks are still not sufficiently confident of a turnaround (in the economies), at least until the end of the year," said Chong Hui Chin, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at J.P. Morgan Chase Bank. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar fell to a one-month low during the session, but managed to trim losses. Late in the local session, the U.S. unit was quoted at S$1.7380, up from S$1.7365 late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  A trader at a European bank in Singapore said there were a lot of U.S. names buying the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pair, continuing a trend seen in the last few days. \par \par \uc2  There's been talk in the market in recent days that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore has been supporting the U.S. dollar, which has damped any enthusiasm to push up the local unit. \par \par \uc2  Talk of such \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  seems to be supported by the recent foreign reserves data, which showed a sharp rise in reserves last month, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  The trader said he believes the government wants to weaken the Singapore dollar to make it more competitive against countries like neighboring Malaysia, whose \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the ringgit, is pegged to the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  The Philippine peso was weighed down by a ratings downgrade from Fitch Ratings, and also as banks bought dollars ahead of a long weekend. However, strong equity inflows into the local stock market put a floor under the peso. \par \par \uc2  The dollar closed at 53.610 pesos on the Philippine Dealing System, up from PHP53.535 Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Fitch lowered the long-term foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rating on the Philippines by a notch to "BB". The move had to a large extent been anticipated as it was reported in a local newspaper in the previous session. \par \par \uc2  Chong of J.P. Morgan Chase Bank, said foreign equity inflows into the Philippine stock market are now more than five times the average in the last 12 months, and such strong flows should help slow the dollar's gains. \par \par \uc2  The key stock index rose 1.9% Thursday to end at its highest close since July 1, 2002. Philippine markets are closed for a holiday Friday. \par \par \uc2  Against the Indonesian rupiah, the dollar was quoted around IDR8,251 late in Asia, up from IDR8,230 Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Market players continued to take profit on the rupiah, which has rallied sharply in recent weeks, amid concerns the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem the rise. \par \par \uc2  Chong said the rupiah is expensive and on a purchasing power parity basis, its fair value should be closer to 10,000 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Still, she said continued interest in the high-yielding \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the momentum of good news in the country should help the rupiah rise to 7,500 by September, although it should then go on to lose ground by year end. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  Thursday cut its overnight money market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate for the second time this month on easing inflation to help spur economic growth. \par \par \uc2  The South Korean won edged up despite official jawboning, although overall activity was quiet as traders believe the government had already \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the previous session to support the dollar at KRW1,190. \par \par \uc2  Exporters, foreigners and players fixing non-deliverable forwards positions all sold the dollar, which closed at KRW1,193.2, down from KRW1,195.4 Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Earlier, Kwon Tae-shin, deputy minister for international affairs at the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Economy, said the government will step in for a "smoothing \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 " anytime when the dollar/won rate fails to reflect the economy's fundamentals, according to Yonhap Infomax. He repeated the same message in the afternoon. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  decided at its monthly monetary policy meeting to keep its overnight call rate target unchanged at 4%, a decision that was widely expected by markets. \par \par \uc2  The New Taiwan dollar was boosted by foreign equity inflows following news that Taiwan Semiconductor Manufacturing Co. would be included in the Philadelphia Stock Exchange's Philly chip index, one of the most widely watched semiconductor indexes in the world. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. unit ended at NT$34.667, down from Wednesday's NT$34.682. \par \par \uc2  The key local stock index rose 1.5% to end at its highest level in more than four months Thursday. Foreign investors net bought nearly NT$3 billion of local shares, which helped underpin the local dollar's gains, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The Thai baht recovered from an early drop to move to a stronger footing. Late in Asia, the dollar was quoted around 41.72 baht, down from THB41.79 Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  -By Nirmala Menon, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-6415-4046; nirmala.menon@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  -Edited by Simon Harvey \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020030612dz6c000md\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
