\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Staying off highs as yen trips. \b0\par\par\uc2 641 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Mai 2003\par 05:57\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Ovais Subhani\par     SINGAPORE, May 9 (Reuters) - Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  remained\par strong against the U.S. dollar on Friday, kept off this week's\par highs by the fear of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but the region weakened\par against the surging euro .\par  As the euro hit four-year highs on the dollar and matched its\par life-high against the yen , the Singapore dollar was\par at its lowest against the euro since it was launched in January\par 1999, and the cross  was heading towards 2.0.\par     Against the U.S. dollar, the Singapore dollar       , Thai\par baht  and the Taiwan dollar were off two-month highs. The\par South Korean won  also eased from a two-month high as\par markets in Seoul resumed trade after a holiday.\par     Even the high yielding Philippine peso        wiped out its\par gains for the week as it fell from an eight month high. The\par Indonesian rupiah  also tripped off an 11-month peak.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Wariness of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  pulled the yen back from 10-month\par highs near 116 yen to around 117 yen on Friday, which also\par weighed on regionals as Japan is a major trade partner for\par Asia.\par     Japanese Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa said yen has\par risen too much, but declined to comment if Japan had\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     Dealers believe most Asian central banks had been buying\par dollars in recent sessions to protect export competitiveness,\par and this had also triggered profit-taking.\par     "Central banks are watchful. They are still assessing the\par impact of SARS on their economies. So they are maintaining some\par caution," said Thio Chin Loo, senior \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  analyst at BNP\par Paribas in Singapore.\par  \par     Still, she said the outlook for Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was\par brighter than that of the yen.\par     "The dollar's downward trend against Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has\par restarted, but they are not likely to rally at the same speed\par as European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," she said.\par     The Singapore dollar eased to around 1.7420 per U.S.\par dollar, before rebounding to around 1.7378, not far from\par Wednesday's two-month high of 1.7365.\par     The Thai baht        fell to around 42.60 per dollar in\par offshore trade before paring some of the losses,  but it\par remained clear of this week's two-month high around 42.40.\par     The peso eased to around 52.40 per dollar, a day after it\par hit 51.88, its strongest since September 13 last year.\par     Dealers in Manila said while remittances from overseas\par workers would offer support, most players were looking to book\par profits before taking fresh positions.\par     The peso is still about five percent higher from its lows\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par above 55 per dollar in March. Its high yields have proved\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par attractive to investors, overshadowing their worries about\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ratings downgrades and the large budget deficit.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Indonesian rupiah , the leading Asian gainer so\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par far this year, pulled back to around 8,600 per dollar from\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Thursday's 11-month high of 8,495.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par On Friday, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central Bank Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  cut its overnight\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rate to 10.75 percent from 11.00 percent.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR AT 0251 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par  Japan yen     117.17       116.35         -0.70\par  Sing dlr      1.7384       1.7381         -0.02\par  Taiwan dlr    34.778       34.716         -0.18\par  Korean won   1199.60      1199.00         -0.05\par  Baht           42.51        42.44         -0.16\par  Peso           52.36        52.15         -0.39\par  Rupiah       8532.00      8555.00         +0.27\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     117.17       118.74         +1.34\par  Sing dlr      1.7384       1.7341         -0.25\par  Taiwan dlr    34.778       34.753         -0.07\par  Korean won   1199.60      1185.80         -1.15\par  Baht           42.51        43.08         +1.34\par  Peso           52.36        53.38         +1.96\par  Rupiah       8532.00      8940.00         +4.78.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030509dz59006y2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
