\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Flows dominate, rupiah surges. \b0\par\par\uc2 750 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Mai 2003\par 11:10\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Vidya Ranganathan\par     SINGAPORE, May 5 (Reuters) - The Indonesian rupiah surged\par to its highest level in over 10 months in holiday-thinned Asian\par trading on Monday, driven by heavy flows believed to be\par offshore investments related to the country's asset sales.\par  \par     Holidays in Japan, China, Korea and Thailand kept trade\par thin.\par     The Singapore dollar rose to a one-month high near 1.7635\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  as a few foreign banks vigorously sold their holdings of U.S. \par \par \uc2  dollars, disregarding a steady Japanese yen and media talk of \par \par \uc2  the government introducing yen-weakening policies. \par \par \uc2  The Philippine peso found renewed strength in data showing \par \par \uc2  strong export growth as Manila markets opened after a Labour \par \par \uc2  Day holiday weekend, but it closed off highs. The peso hit a \par \par \uc2  high of 52.235, a level last seen two weeks back. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah struck 8,618, last traded at the end of June \par \par \uc2  2002. A trader in Jakarta said it was likely offshore players \par \par \uc2  had brought into the country funds meant for investing in the \par \par \uc2  Indonesian Bank Restructuring Agency's (IBRA) sale of a \par \par \uc2  majority stake in Bank Danamon. \par \par \uc2  Monday was the deadline for final bids. IBRA had earlier \par \par \uc2  said there were three bidders - a consortium led by \par \par \uc2  Singapore's Temasek Holdings, a group led by Bhakti Capital \par \par \uc2  Indonesia and including Bank Mega, and another group including \par \par \uc2  Bank Artha Graha. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     Traders said there were few signs the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to contain the rupiah's rise.\par     "Inflation has come lower, so they can allow the rupiah to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par appreciate in nominal terms," said Bhanu Baweja, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par strategist with UBS Warburg. Baweja said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  might have been \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The rupiah has gained 6.1 percent in 1-= months, and in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par April Indonesia's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves increased by one\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par billion dollars to $33.6 billion, after rising by $4.7 billion\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in the 12 months before that.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SARS DATA BOOSTS SING DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Traders said aggressive position-squaring propped up the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Singapore dollar and drove it to a one-month high after some\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par players considered it excessively weak given the slowly\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par improving outlook on the Severe Acute Respiratory Syndrome\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (SARS) epidemic.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "I imagine that a good chunk of that is position-squaring,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par because SARS news has been better for the past week or so,"\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par said James Malcolm, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at JP Morgan.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "We'd continue to recommend selling U.S. dollars. The\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par mid-point of our band doesn't come in until 1.7300, so we have\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par a long way to go before we're back at the mid-point," he said,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par referring to the undisclosed trade-weighted band authorities\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par manage the Sing dollar in.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par There were no fresh cases of SARS in Singapore and new\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par cases dropped in Hong Kong. Worldwide, deaths from the virus\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rose to over 460 people, and the number infected climbed to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par almost 7,000.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Meanwhile, amid expectations the U.S. Federal Reserve would\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par leave rates unchanged at its meeting this week, analysts\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par expected the rally in high-yielding \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , such as some\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Latin Americans, the South African rand, Australian dollar and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Indonesian rupiah, would continue but with less momentum.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par JP Morgan's Malcolm warned local markets could be a bit\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par nervous after the light sell-off seen in other emerging markets\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par last week. The Brazilian real and South African rand were sold\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par last week after some rather steep rallies.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     But a spillover of that kind of profit-taking was unlikely,\par he said.\par     "Those markets have been very heavily bought in the past\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par couple of weeks. And, those are not the sensitivities or\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par overhangs we have in Asia at the moment, so the impetus for\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par profit-taking in Asia is much more modest."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Taiwan dollar stuck to a very thin range around 34.80,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par with neighbours Japan and Korea shut for holidays.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR AT 0840 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen     118.96       118.84         -0.10\par  Sing dlr      1.7640       1.7695         +0.31\par  Taiwan dlr    34.801       34.812         +0.03\par  Peso           52.51        52.55         +0.08\par  Rupiah       8620.00      8658.00         +0.44\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     118.96       118.74         -0.18\par  Sing dlr      1.7640       1.7341         -1.70\par  Taiwan dlr    34.801       34.753         -0.14\par  Peso           52.51        53.38         +1.66\par  Rupiah       8620.00      8940.00         +3.71.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030505dz5500itt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
