\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Up in volatile, war-driven trade. \b0\par\par\uc2 666 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 April 2003\par 11:29\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Vidya Ranganathan\par     SINGAPORE, April 8 (Reuters) - Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were mostly\par higher late on Tuesday after a volatile session driven\par primarily by news from the Iraq war and worries over the spread\par of SARS.\par     The Singapore dollar       , Thai baht        and Taiwan\par dollar  were choppy, following the lead of the Japanese\par yen , amid reports the U.S. military had bombed a target\par in Baghdad where Iraqi President Saddam Hussein may have been.\par     Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  also grappled with anxiety over the Severe\par Acute Respiratory Syndrome (SARS) virus, which has claimed over\par 100 human lives and has infected over 2,700 people.\par     "In the near-term, the market will continue to trade on how\par the war is shaping up in Iraq," DBS Bank economist Lee Boon\par Keng said in a commentary.\par     "And we expect the victory dance to stay for a little\par longer.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Hence, the dollar will stay relatively well-bid, and\par bonds will continue to face downside pressure."\par  \par     The Singapore dollar spent most of the day around 1.78 per\par dollar, clear of Monday's five-month lows near 1.7850.\par     Still, markets worried about the prime minister's remark\par that the SARS could cut growth in China, Hong Kong and\par Singapore by as much as one percent.\par     Speculation was also rife over whether the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary\par \f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 \par Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore would tolerate a Singapore dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par outside the weaker end of the undisclosed trade-weighted band\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par it is managed in.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     "There is a possibility they will consider these kind of\par measures," said Thio Chin Loo, strategist with BNP Paribas.\par     "Given there is also volatility with this war, the\par justification for a wider band is there."\par     The Thai baht        fell to a 3-=   month low of 43.24 per\par dollar in offshore deals, rallied and then weakened again as\par local markets resumed after a holiday.\par     One-year forwards on the Hong Kong dollar peg\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par hugged 200 points, coming off an early high of 210 basis\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par points. The forwards rose markedly last week on market talk\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SARS could put pressure on Hong Kong's economy, its reserves\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and hence the HK dollar peg.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may not react very positively to the end\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of the war because there still are a few risk factors such as\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par North Korea and SARS that loom over this region," UBS Warburg's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par strategist Bhanu Baweja said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     PESO, RUPIAH INDIFFERENT\par     The Philippine peso        opened steady, and then extended\par its three-week uptrend to close at a 3-=   month high of 52.88,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par indifferent not just to the regional swings but also to news\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par that the government had overshot its first quarter budget\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par deficit target by 10 percent.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Indonesian rupiah  was surprisingly strong even\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  cut rates. Bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  cut its\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par overnight \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rate by 25 basis points to 11.25 percent\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par on Monday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Korean won             and Taiwan dollar mimicked\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the early gains in the yen, but markets were suspicious of the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par won's gains amid expectations the North Korean risk will\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par escalate ahead of a U.N. Security Council debate on the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par country's suspected nuclear arms programme this week.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR AT 0845 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen     119.56       120.73         +0.98\par  Sing dlr      1.7811       1.7821         +0.06\par  Taiwan dlr    34.822       34.812         -0.03\par  Korean won   1253.30      1258.30         +0.40\par  Baht           43.08        43.17         +0.21\par  Peso           52.85        53.25         +0.70\par  Rupiah       8873.00      8892.00         +0.21\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     119.56       118.74         -0.69\par  Sing dlr      1.7811       1.7341         -2.64\par  Taiwan dlr    34.822       34.753         -0.20\par  Korean won   1253.30      1185.80         -5.39\par  Baht           43.08        43.08          0.00\par  Peso           52.85        53.38         +0.95\par  Rupiah       8873.00      8940.00         +0.76.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030408dz4800jal\par }\page {\par\fs