\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia \highlight\uc2  Rupiah Ends Up; Talks Of Ctrl Bk  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 250 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2003\par 10:37\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2003, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA -(Dow Jones)- The Indonesian rupiah ended slightly higher against the dollar Monday on talks of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up the local unit, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar closed at IDR8,955, down from its close Friday at IDR8,965. The dollar rose to its intraday high of IDR8,995 earlier Monday on warnings by the U.S. and U.K. over the weekend that terrorists may launch an attack on their citizens in Indonesia due to the war in Iraq. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said Bank Indonesia was heard offering the dollar when the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moved close to the psychologically important IDR9,000 level. \par \par \uc2  The government is aiming for an average dollar exchange rate of IDR9,000 this year. \par \par \uc2  Besides suspected Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the dollar also gave up its early gains because anti-Western protests in the world's most populous Muslim country have remained orderly so far. \par \par \uc2  "There are far bigger protests in other parts of the world, so I don't think protests here will necessarily irk the market," said a dealer with a foreign bank in Jakarta. \par \par \uc2  Most market participants, however, still chose to stay on the sidelines as it remains unclear how long the Iraq war will last. \par \par \uc2  Dealers expect the dollar to trade between IDR8,900 and IDR9,000 Tuesday. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By I Made Sentana, Dow Jones Newswires; 62-21 39831277;\par I-Made.Sentana@dowjones.com\par \f28 \pa