\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesia Rupiah Ends Lower On Mounting Iraq War Fears \b0\par\par\uc2 277 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2003\par 10:37\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2003, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA -(Dow Jones)- The Indonesian rupiah lost more ground against the U.S. dollar in thin dealings Monday as the market braced for a likely U.S.-led military attack on Iraq, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar closed at 8,965 rupiah, up from its close Friday at IDR8,915 as the market anticipated widespread anti-West protests in Indonesia, the world's most populous Muslim country, if Iraq is attacked. \par \par \uc2  Anti-West protests are expected to further deter foreign investors from coming to Indonesia. \par \par \uc2  U.S. President George W. Bush, with summit partners from the U.K. and Spain, over the weekend gave the United Nations a Monday deadline to endorse the use of force to compel Iraq's immediate disarmament, calling Monday "a moment of truth for the world." \par \par \uc2  Dealers suspected that Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market Monday but failed to arrest the dollar's rise as the amount of dollars it sold was meager. \par \par \uc2  The dollar is expected to test the psychologically-key barrier of IDR9,000 Tuesday if the nation's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  isn't more active in supporting the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Still, capital inflows linked to government asset sales would help fend off some of the selling pressure facing the rupiah, they added. \par \par \uc2  The Indonesian Bank Restructuring Agency is in the midst of selling a 50% stake in Bank Danamon to strategic investors. Deutsche Bank, the Singapore government's investment arm Temasek Holdings, and HSBC are among the bidders. \par \par \uc2  -By I Made 