\par\par \b \uc2  Bank Indonesia Says To Continue Cutting Rates Gradually \b0\par\par\uc2 202 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2003\par 02:27\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2003, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA -(Dow Jones)- Indonesia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Tuesday that it will continue to cut interest rates gradually as inflationary pressure continues to ease and with the rupiah likely to remain stable versus the dollar. \par \par \uc2  "The monetary policy will continue to be able to accommodate a gradual and cautious rate cut," Bank Indonesia said in a statement following a monthly meeting of its board of governors late Monday. \par \par \uc2  Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  Friday cut its key money market rate, the overnight \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate, to 11.500% from 12.125%. \par \par \uc2  The rate cut followed a fall in inflation to 7.34% on year in February from 8.74% in January. \par \par \uc2  Indonesia's government has been pressing for lower rates to help spur economic growth at a time when unemployment is rising and threatening social unrest. \par \par \uc2  The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been stable as capital inflows linked to government asset sales has helped mitigate the damaging impact of fears over an Iraq war. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was trading at 8,885 rupiah at 0136 GMT, unchanged from its close Monday. \par \par \uc2  -By I Made Sentana, Dow Jones Newswires; 62-21 39831277 I-Made.Sentana@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  -Edited by Simon Harvey \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020030311dz3b0002r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
