\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesia Rupiah Ends Up On Threat Of  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Action \b0\par\par\uc2 147 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Februar 2003\par 09:59\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2003, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA -(Dow Jones)- The Indonesian rupiah ended slightly higher Friday as market participants cut their dollar positions ahead of the weekend amid the threat of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The dollar ended at 8,930 rupiah, down from its close Thursday at IDR8,945. \par \par \uc2  Investors bought dollars strongly this weak amid fears a war on Iraq will spark anti-U.S. demonstrations, hurting the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  But the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was unable to sustain its gains in thin trade with the overhanging threat of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold dollars earlier this week to temper the dollar's rise but wasn't active Friday, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers expect the dollar to trade between IDR8,900 and IDR9,000 next week. \par \par \uc2  -By Tom Wright, Dow Jones Newswires; 62-21 39831277; Tom.Wright@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1159 1848 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020030214dz2e000jd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
