\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesia Rupiah Ends Slightly Higher On Dlr Pft-Taking \b0\par\par\uc2 197 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Februar 2003\par 10:08\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2003, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA -(Dow Jones)- The Indonesian rupiah ended slightly higher Thursday on dollar profit-taking, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  closed at 8,945 rupiah, down from its close Tuesday at IDR8,980. Local markets were closed Wednesday for a public holiday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the dollar rose to an intraday high of IDR8,985 early Thursday on corporate demand. But expectations that Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  - the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  - would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to help the local unit discouraged market participants from pushing the dollar higher. Instead, they took profits. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said sentiment toward the rupiah remains cautious due to Iraq jitters. Analysts are concerned that military action by the U.S. and its Western allies against Iraq could spark anti-Western sentiment in Indonesia, which could jeopardize foreign capital inflows. \par \par \uc2  Indonesia is in dire need of fresh investments as domestic consumption - which has driven the nation's economic recovery in the last three years - shows signs of weakening, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers expect the dollar to trade between IDR8,925 and IDR8,975 Friday. \par \par \uc2  -By I Made Sentana, Dow Jones Newswires; 62-21 39831277; I-Made.Sentana@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1159 1848 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020030213dz2d000jv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
