\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesia Rupiah Ends Up Amid Talk Of State Bk Dlr Sales \b0\par\par\uc2 234 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 November 2002\par 10:30\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA -(Dow Jones)- The Indonesian rupiah closed higher Wednesday as state-owned banks sold dollars, likely on behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar ended at 9,055 rupiah, down from Tuesday's close of IDR9,085. \par \par \uc2  Dealers suspected Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  via state banks to drag the dollar down to the level before the Bali bombings last month, at around IDR9,000. \par \par \uc2  Pushing the dollar lower will leave room for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to guide its benchmark interest rate lower to help reduce the costs the government shoulders to bail out the local banking system. \par \par \uc2  Indeed, Bank Indonesia in a weekly auction Wednesday cut the weighted average rate of its one-month Sertifikat Bank Indonesia notes to 13.08% from 13.10%. It's the first drop after the Bali blasts. \par \par \uc2  Dealers added that offshore participants also continued to unwind their long-dollar positions as the police make inroads on the Bali bombing probe. \par \par \uc2  Dealers expect the dollar to head down to IDR9,000 Thursday. Any upward move is expected to stall near IDR9,100. \par \par \uc2  They said the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  will stabilize around IDR9,000 before fresh demand ahead of the year-end drives it higher again to IDR9,500. \par \par \uc2  -By I Made Sentana, Dow Jones Newswires; 62-21 39831277; I-Made.Sentana@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1159 1848 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020021113dybd000nb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pn