\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Easier bias, peso at 14-month low. \b0\par\par\uc2 742 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Oktober 2002\par 11:04\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Ovais Subhani\par     SINGAPORE, Oct 18 (Reuters) - Security concerns and\par economic worries pushed the Philippine peso to a fresh 14-month\par low on Friday, as most Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  treaded narrow ranges\par with a weaker bias.\par     The peso fell to 53.29 per dollar, a low since August 2001,\par on early news of a grenade explosion in Manila's main financial\par district, a day after a deadly bombing in southern Philippines.\par     Also discouraging was data showing a trade deficit of $174\par million in August after three months of surpluses, backing the\par view that exports were losing momentum.\par  \par     Philippine \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Deputy Governor Amando Tetangco\par said the bank would \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  if necessary to ensure stability.\par     "We are monitoring market movements. We have a flexible\par exchange rate policy but we will take measures if necessary to\par maintain orderly market conditions," Tetangco told reporters.\par     Dealers in Manila said talk of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  checking\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  rates with local banks offered some support. However, as there \par \par \uc2  was no actual \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dollar bids by local corporates \par \par \uc2  just above 53.24 kept the peso under pressure in late trade. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     James Malcolm, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at JP Morgan Chase in\par Singapore, said the oversold peso's downside was limited.\par     "Offshore investors are long dollars and importers are well\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par hedged," he said, adding rising remittances from overseas\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par workers ahead of Christmas would also provide some near term\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par support.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par BAHT STEADY\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Rumours about \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  activity kept the Thai baht in a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par tight range around 43.75, as dollar purchases from foreign\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par names absorbed sales, mainly from exporters and other local\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par players selling some dollar holdings built earlier in the week.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers in Bangkok said amid lack of fresh local leads, the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par market was waiting for strong trading cues from the yen and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Singapore dollar before pushing the baht further down.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par They said no activity from the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was spotted,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par but players were cautious on rumours the Bank of Thailand was\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in the offshore market late Thursday to buy dollars at around\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 43.70.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     The Bank of Thailand's monetary policy committee has a\par scheduled meeting on Monday.\par     The Indonesian rupiah lingered around 9,000-9,225, with its\par downside supported by dollar sales from local names, suspected\par to be acting on behalf of authorities.\par     Bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's deputy governor Miranda Goeltom said the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par bank would \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market if\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par necessary and that it wanted the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to strengthen beyond\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 9,000.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers in Jakarta said there was little price action in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par response to those comments, but players were likely to be more\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par cautious on the downside after the deadly bombings on Bali last\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par weekend heightened worries about regional security.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had admitted selling dollars to prop up\par the rupiah after it hit a six-month low around 9,400 on Monday.\par     The Singapore dollar slipped to touch a session low of\par 1.7928, from an early high of 1.7864 and a near two-week high\par of 1.7790 hit in overnight offshore trade.\par     But dollar offers beyond 1.7900, from players squaring\par stale dollar positions, limited its downside, dealers said.\par     The Taiwan dollar ended onshore trade down at 34.928, after\par hitting a three-week high of 34.791 on equity-related dollar\par inflows.\par     Dealers in Singapore said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was again\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par spotted buying dollars cap exchange rate gains, to maintain\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par export competitiveness in the face of declines in other\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par regionals.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Korean won eased to a low of 1,247.5 in onshore trade,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par although dollar sales by foreign equity funds limited the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par decline.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S.       $0839 GMT\p