\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Heavy losses after Bali blasts. \b0\par\par\uc2 601 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Oktober 2002\par 11:09\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, Oct 14 (Reuters) - The Indonesian rupiah's plunge to a 5-= month low after weekend bomb blasts in Bali raised concerns over security and risk-aversion in Asia, forcing other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to fresh lows on Monday. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah fell to 9,350 per dollar, down 3.6 percent on the day, a level last seen in April, only recovering after \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  around 9,300. \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's stock market had fallen 10 percent by late afternoon. \par \par \uc2  Traders anxiously bought up the dollar against the Philippine peso , which was seen as vulnerable to security threats and was placed on high alert following the blasts, and the Singapore dollar , seen exposed if foreign businesses shift out of Asia. \par \par \uc2  Moreover, there was disheartening data from the United States on Friday showing retail sales fell more than anticipated and consumer sentiment hit a nine-year low. \par \par \uc2  "While Asian countries' current account surpluses have kept their asset markets and \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  fairly buffered from risk-aversion flows and from contagion from Latin America's woes year-to-date, fears of heightened security risk are likely to weigh on regionals," UBS Warburg said in a market commentary. \par \par \uc2  By afternoon, regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were marginally off their lows but substantially weaker than Friday's finish, while stock markets in Thailand and Philippines ended down, as traders assessed the impact of the blasts. \par \par \uc2  No one has claimed responsibility for the bombs late Saturday night in Bali. The explosions ripped through packed nightclubs popular with foreign tourists and killed at least 183 people. \par \par \uc2  Traders also felt market reaction had been subdued, with trade thinned by holidays in Japan and Hong Kong. The U.S. bond market is also shut on Monday. \par \par \uc2  MULTI-MONTH LOWS \par \par \uc2  The Thai baht tested early February lows at 44.02 per dollar and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  denied market talk that it had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The peso extended 14-month lows and slipped past 53 to 53.05, ending close to those lows. \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar slide past Friday's close at a 15-year low of 35.157 and hit a low of 35.21. \par \par \uc2  Global growth concerns and a drop in the Korean consumer outlook to a nine-month low weighed on the won , although stock purchases by foreign investors buoyed the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to a firmer close. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar bounced off a five-month low of 1.8025 and clambered back towards 1.79 as other regionals recovered. \par \par \uc2  A JP Morgan note said any weakness in the rupiah could have a heavy impact on the Sing dollar, given the rupiah was a key component of the trade-weighted index against which Singapore is believed to manage its exchange rate. \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR AT 0900 GMT Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par   Japan yen     124.02       124.08         +0.05\par   Sing dlr      1.7983       1.7929         -0.30\par   Taiwan dlr    35.168       35.157         -0.03\par   Korean won   1258.80      1258.80         +0.00\par   Baht           43.97        43.85         -0.27\par   P