\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesia Rupiah Ends At 5-Mo Low Vs Dlr On Bali Bombings \b0\par\par\uc2 393 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Oktober 2002\par 11:43\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA -(Dow Jones)- The Indonesian rupiah took a severe drumming against the dollar Monday, closing at a five-month low in a volatile session after the weekend terrorist attacks on the island of Bali. \par \par \uc2  The dollar rose to an intraday high of 9,350 rupiah earlier in the day but slipped back slightly to close at a five-month high of IDR9,330 as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 . That was 3.4% higher than its close Friday at IDR9,010. \par \par \uc2  The Saturday night attack on a nightclub packed with Western tourists on Bali has further undermined investor confidence toward Indonesia, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  The attacks could adversely affect Indonesia's economy and influence the politics of the country, Standard & Poor's Corp. said in a press release Monday. \par \par \uc2  "The government's response to the fatal bombing, which killed more than 180 people, has implications for policy direction, and potentially the result of elections due next year. To a more limited extent, the incident could have fiscal and economic implications," it added. \par \par \uc2  The dollar came off its intraday high after Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to sell the dollar. Confirming its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in a statement it will continue to monitor the rupiah and will act if necessary to keep its level stable. \par \par \uc2  It didn't mention how much it sold in the local foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, but dealers reckoned it sold between $15 million and $20 million. Dealers also alleged that the Indonesian Bank Restructuring Agency joined forces with Bank Indonesia to help the local unit. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they expect the dollar to test IDR9,400 resistance Tuesday as foreign investors are expected to buy the dollar in the coming days after they unloaded Indonesian stocks Monday. \par \par \uc2  The Indonesian stock market main index fell 38.991 points, or 10.36%, to close at a four-year low of 337.475. \par \par \uc2  Bank Indonesia is expected to try to defend the rupiah again. But dealers doubt if it will be successful given the extent of the blow on the Indonesian economy from the attacks. \par \par \uc2  Many \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategists predict the dollar to close around IDR10,000 by the end of the year. \par \par \uc2  -By I Made Sentana, Dow Jones Newswires; 62-21 39831277; I-Made.Sentana@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1159 1848 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020021014dyae000ha\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
