\par\par \b \uc2  Bk Indonesia Says Monitoring Rupiah Movements After Bomb \b0\par\par\uc2 203 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Oktober 2002\par 08:40\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA -(Dow Jones)- \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  confirmed it had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to help the rupiah Monday after a weekend bomb explosion in Bali, which killed at least 188 people, pushed the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to a five-month low. \par \par \uc2  Bank Indonesia, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said in a statement it will continue to monitor the rupiah and will act if necessary to keep its level stable. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has ample \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves of around $30 billion," the statement said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar moved to an intraday high at IDR9,350 before coming back to around IDR9,225 and IDR9,250 in the afternoon after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the Indonesian Bank Restructuring Agency \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell dollars through the market. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  didn't say how many dollars it sold, but traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was between $15 million and $20 million. \par \par \uc2  Despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , analysts expect the rupiah to lose ground in coming weeks on concerns over security after the blast. \par \par \uc2  Indonesia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't have enough reserves to defend the market against a broad selling of the rupiah, traders said. \par \par \uc2  -