\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesia Rupiah Ends Flat; Suspected  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Action \b0\par\par\uc2 222 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Oktober 2002\par 11:38\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA -(Dow Jones)- The Indonesian rupiah ended flat Monday with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  allegedly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to stem the dollar's gains amid general dollar strength versus most other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar closed at 9,015 rupiah, unchanged from its close Thursday. Markets were closed Friday for a public holiday. The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traded between IDR9,012 and IDR9,020 Monday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said Bank Indonesia was suspected to have been in the market to cap the dollar's rise Monday but it has a a policy of not commenting on specific \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  is suspected to have been in the market on almost every trading day since late last month. \par \par \uc2  The government's average dollar exchange rate target is IDR9,000 for this year, which analysts say will be hard to achieve. \par \par \uc2  Overall trading was thin as the market still lacked fresh incentives, dealers said. They estimated trading volume stood at $60 million Monday compared with an average of around $150 million during relatively lively trading. \par \par \uc2  Dealers expect the dollar to move between IDR9,010 and IDR9,030 Tuesday unless new incentives emerge from which to aggressively trade off. \par \par \uc2  -By I Made Sentana, Dow Jones Newswires; 62-21 39831277; I-Made.Sentana@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1159 1848 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020021007dya7000j6\par }\p