\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia \highlight\uc2  Rupiah Ends Flat; Reported Ctrl Bk  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 294 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Oktober 2002\par 12:40\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA -(Dow Jones)- The Indonesian rupiah ended flat Wednesday as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reportedly sold dollars to offset both dollar demand by local companies and the knock-on effect of a rising dollar against other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar closed at 9,015 unchanged from its close Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The settlement date for Wednesday's spot transactions will be Monday - instead of Friday, as the market will be closed for a public holiday Friday. \par \par \uc2  The dollar earlier Wednesday rallied to an intraday high of IDR9,030 as foreign banks in Jakarta covered their dollar-short positions, spooked by the dollar's gains versus the yen. Local companies jumped on the bandwagon later to buy the dollar for offshore debt repayment. \par \par \uc2  Bank Indonesia, however, was suspected of selling the dollar through state banks to support the rupiah. \par \par \uc2  Dealers expect upward pressure on the dollar to persist Thursday due to its expected sustained bullishness against the yen. Bank Indonesia, however, is expected to steadfastly support the rupiah. \par \par \uc2  Dealers expect the dollar to trade between IDR9,005 and IDR9,035 Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, Bank Indonesia cut the benchmark weighted average rate of its one-month Sertifikat Bank Indonesia notes to 13.06% in a weekly auction from 13.22%. The rate cut showed the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's resolve to guide the rate lower to around 12% by year end, dealers said. The pace of the rate cut, however, slowed down after the official statistics bureau warned Tuesday that inflation is set to rise during the last three months of the year due to religious festivities and Monday's fuel price hike. \par \par \uc2  -By I Made Sentana,Dow Jones Newswires;62-21 39831277 I-Made.Sentana@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1159 1848 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020021002dya2000m1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
