\par\par \b \uc2  Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Up Late On Yen, Dlr Sales By Exporters \b0\par\par\uc2  By Nirmala Menon \par \uc2 784 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 September 2002\par 12:32\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Of Dow Jones Newswires \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were lifted along with the yen late Monday after the dollar slid following the ouster of Japan's top banking regulator who was known to oppose a publicly funded cleanup of banks' bad loans \par \par \uc2  The Korean won and the New Taiwan dollar also gained from end-of-month dollar sales by exporters. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  shed more than a yen and a half in Asia on heavy selling by U.S. and European funds that correctly bet top bank regulator Hakuo Yanagisawa would be removed in a Cabinet reshuffle. \par \par \uc2  In a surprise move, he was replaced with Heizo Takenaka, one of the most vocal proponents of a stepped-up bank cleanup. \par \par \uc2  Coupled with dollar sales by exporters, the U.S. unit sank to an 11-day low of Y121.12 in Asia. \par \par \uc2  Claudio Piron, Singapore-based head of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy at Standard Chartered Bank, said market players may also be betting Japan would take other surprise action going forward, which would be positive for the yen. \par \par \uc2  By extension, that would mean more upside for regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , especially the Singapore dollar and the Korean won which most closely track the yen, he said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar ended nearly flat at 1,227.8 won from KRW1,227.9 Friday as the South Korean unit recouped early losses in the wake of the yen's strength. \par \par \uc2  The session was initially marked by strong demand for dollars due to large-scale short-covering by banks, which took the U.S. unit to a day's high of KRW1,233.0. \par \par \uc2  But the dollar's subsequent decline against the yen, coupled with end-of-month sales of the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by local exporters helped the won recover, traders said. \par \par \uc2  In Singapore, market participants took their cue from the yen's firm tone to unwind long dollar positions. \par \par \uc2  The dollar sellers were mainly U.S. and Japanese investment houses that had built up long positions since Friday, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The market players had to cut these positions to minimize losses following the sharp fall on Wall Street Friday, they added. \par \par \uc2  But trading was thin amid continued uncertainty over the U.S. economy, the city state's biggest export market. \par \par \uc2  Against the Singapore dollar, the U.S. unit was quoted around S$1.7778 late in Asia, from S$1.7782 Friday. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, Taiwan exporters also sold the U.S. unit for local dollars to pay salaries or cover other expenses, traders said. \par \par \uc2  That, together with the yen's strength, helped the New Taiwan dollar recover from early losses that were caused partly by the exit of foreign equity funds and the yen's initial weakness. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar ended at NT$34.918, slightly down from Friday's NT$34.921. \par \par \uc2  Intraday, the dollar reached a peak of NT$34.980, and hit a trough at NT$34.913. \par \par \uc2  The island's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which regularly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to prevent any sharp movement of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was largely quiet Monday, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The Philippine peso was also buoyed by the yen-led rise of regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  although trading volume was almost flat, indicating mild activity. \par \par \uc2  But activity in the black market was reportedly strong. One bank trader said the dollar was traded between PHP52.55 and PHP52.63 in the parallel market. \par \par \uc2  Some dollar buyers may have opted to go there to skip documentation required by banks and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , another bank trader said. \par \par \uc2  On the Philippine Dealing System however, the dollar closed at PHP52.400, slightly down from PHP52.460 Friday, after moving between PHP52.385 and PHP52.450. \par \par \uc2  Trading volume was hardly changed at $83.7 million, from S$83.1 million previously. \par \par \uc2  In \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was again suspected of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the rupiah, helping to counter further negative news which took the dollar to its intraday high of IDR9,017 early in the session. \par \par \uc2  News that soldiers had opened fire on police on the island of Sumatra, leaving four police dead, helped keep the dollar well bought, traders said. \par \par \uc2  But Bank Indonesia, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was reported to sell about $5 million through state banks, with thin volumes aiding in pushing the dollar lower. \par \par \uc2  The dollar ended at its intraday low of IDR9,000, from IDR9,015 Friday. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, the dollar was also weaker against the Thai baht, in line with the regional trend. \par \par \uc2  Late in Asia, the dollar was quoted around THB43.40, from THB43.43 late Friday. \par \par \uc2  -By Nirmala Menon, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-6415-4046; nirmala.menon@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020020930dy9u000r6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
