\par\par \b \uc2  Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Down Late On Yen, HK$ Peg Speculation \b0\par\par\uc2 792 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 September 2002\par 11:46\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- A weak yen and renewed speculation of a delinking of the Hong Kong dollar from the U.S. unit drove Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  lower Friday, with the Philippine peso closing at its lowest in over a year. \par \par \uc2  The first ever undersubscription of a 10-year Japanese government bond auction highlighted uncertainty about Japan's economic policy and weighed on the yen, which broadly sets the trend for regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the dollar is also plagued with its own problems, given weak economic data from the U.S., falling stock prices and continued fears of a war with Iraq. \par \par \uc2  So, the broader picture lies in "trying to work out which of the major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to dislike the least," commented David Simmonds, senior emerging markets strategist for Asia at The Royal Bank of Scotland. \par \par \uc2  Although the yen's movements against the dollar was the main driving force in regional markets, revival of talk that the Hong Kong authorities may abandon the local dollar's 7.8 peg to the U.S. unit created a buzz in the early in the trading session. \par \par \uc2  The speculation, which sent premiums on one-year Hong Kong dollar forwards soaring, was fanned by a Hong Kong news report on lawmaker Emily Lau's request for a study of the peg. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar and the Thai baht faced mild selling pressure on the speculation, which was largely dismissed by analysts and traders. \par \par \uc2  However, "most investors are holding on to the dollar amid the uncertainties," a trader said. \par \par \uc2  The Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  later issued a statement saying the government "has clearly stated that it has no plan to change the linked exchange rate system," while Lau told Dow Jones Newswires that she was appalled by the furor and was ready to support abandoning the proposed study. \par \par \uc2  Late in Asia, the U.S. dollar was quoted around $1.7796 against the Singapore unit, from $1.7693 late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Activity was moderate as market participants remain uncertain about the U.S. dollar's near-term direction on lingering concerns of a possible war between the U.S. and Iraq, traders said. \par \par \uc2  In the Philippines, the dollar ended at 52.475 pesos on the Philippine Dealing System - its highest finish since Aug. 9, 2001 - from PHP52.285 Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Volume jumped to $118 million from $76 million. \par \par \uc2  Despite an initial dip to PHP52.35 in early trading, the dollar climbed steadily for the rest of the day, hitting an intraday high of PHP52.49. \par \par \uc2  "The peso simply tracked the depreciating yen," said a trader at a local bank. \par \par \uc2  Against the New Taiwan dollar, the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  ended at 34.772, up from NT$34.620 at the previous session close, after trading between NT$34.670 and NT$34.780 intraday. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the local dollar tracked the yen, as it often does due to close trade ties between Japan and Taiwan, and also because they have similar export markets. \par \par \uc2  A rise in equity-related outflows, which increased demand for the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , also weighed on the local dollar, a dealer said. The Weighted Price Index of the Taiwan Stock Exchange fell 1.4% to a fresh 2002 low of 4429.25 points Friday. \par \par \uc2  However, traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to shore up the local unit by selling U.S. dollars at around NT$34.75. \par \par \uc2  In \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the rupiah, which fell as low as 9,040 after Thursday's sharp decline on the stock market. \par \par \uc2  The dollar closed Asian trading at IDR9,030 up from IDR9,005 Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has a policy of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  but never confirms specific actions. Recently, it said it's happy with the dollar trading below IDR9,000. \par \par \uc2  All eyes are now on the likelihood of a U.S. led war on Iraq, which is widely seen as a danger for security in Indonesia, the world's most populous Muslim country. The U.S. claims a number of militant groups with al-Qaida links are operating in the country. \par \par \uc2  As a result, even though higher oil prices in the event of war means better export earnings for Indonesia, it could also put off investors from returning to the country. Indonesia is Asia's only member of the Organization of Petroleum Exporting Countries. \par \par \uc2  The dollar also climbed against the Thai baht in line with the regional trend, closing the Asian session at THB43.32 baht, up from THB43.02 Thursday. \par \par \uc2  South Korea's financial markets were closed Friday for Chuseok, or the local Thanksgiving holiday. \par \par \uc2  -By Nirmala Menon, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-6415-4046; nirmala.menon@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020020920dy9k000lb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
