\par\par \b \uc2  Bk  \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia \highlight\uc2 : Monitoring Rupiah Weakness, May  \highlight22\uc2 Intervene \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 147 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 September 2002\par 09:44\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA -(Dow Jones)- Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said Monday it is monitoring the rupiah's weakening trend against the dollar and may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if necessary. \par \par \uc2  "If the rupiah keeps falling we may do something including \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Deputy Governor Miranda Gultom told reporters. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  wasn't active in the market Monday. Gultom made no comment on this. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah's weakness Monday was mainly due to a fall in regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and uncertainty over the build up to a possible U.S. strike against Iraq, she said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar is trading at IDR9,060 near the close of trading Monday, up from IDR8,965 late Friday. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had previously drawn IDR9,000 as a line it will defend. \par \par \uc2  -By Farida Husna, Dow Jones Newswires; 6221 3983 1277; farida.husna@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020020916dy9g000ec\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
