\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesia Rupiah Ends Dn, But Off Lows On Ctrl Bk Action \b0\par\par\uc2 336 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 September 2002\par 11:28\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA -(Dow Jones)- The Indonesian rupiah ended lower Wednesday, but off its lows as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was rumored to have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market. \par \par \uc2  The dollar's strength against regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  - and local demand for the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from companies with foreign debt - helped push the rupiah lower. \par \par \uc2  The dollar closed at IDR8,890, up from IDR8,865 at the close of Asian trading Tuesday. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar-selling helped pull the dollar back from its intraday high at IDR8,905, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , has a policy of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market but never comments on specific actions. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to trade in a range between IDR8,975 and IDR8,925 Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  auctioned its one-month Sertifikat Bank Indonesia note Wednesday at an average yield of 13.78%, down from 14.07% last week. \par \par \uc2  Indonesian authorities are hoping lower rates will spur growth. Finance Minister Boediono said Wednesday the country was likely to meet its 4% economic growth target this year. But experts, including the World Bank, warn the country needs at least 6% growth to create enough work for new job seekers each year. \par \par \uc2  Bank Indonesia's board of governors said in a statement earlier Wednesday that it hopes to keep cutting rates due to benign inflation, and a stronger rupiah. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah didn't move on the news as sentiment is barely affected by interest rate policy. The country's banking system is still majority owned by the state, with huge non-performing loans. That means lower rates won't necessarily translate to greater loan growth immediately. \par \par \uc2  Still, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also said new loans in August had jumped 25% on month, a positive sign for the banking system, which needs to look for new ways to make money now that rates are falling. \par \par \uc2  -By Tom Wright, Dow Jones Newswires; 6221 3983 1277; tom.wright@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1159 1848 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020020911dy9b000jl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
