\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesia Rupiah Ends Lower As Local Shares Fall \b0\par\par\uc2 275 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 September 2002\par 11:43\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA -(Dow Jones)- The Indonesian rupiah ended lower Wednesday as the local stock market lost ground. \par \par \uc2  Dollar demand from local companies repaying foreign debt also helped keep the rupiah on the downside. \par \par \uc2  The dollar ended Asian trade at 8,865 rupiah, higher than IDR8,840 at Tuesday's close. \par \par \uc2  The JSX Composite Index ended down 2.2%, or 9.546 points, at 420.442, following losses on Wall Street overnight. \par \par \uc2  Still, the dollar isn't expected to trade much higher due to its generally weak tone against other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the region, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Also, \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to shore up the rupiah versus the dollar around IDR8,890, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Any \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to bolster the rupiah is expected to counter demand for the dollar by companies looking to repay huge offshore debts - an overhang from the 1997-98 Asian crisis - and so keep the dollar/rupiah rate in a very tight range for the rest of this week, traders added. \par \par \uc2  Bank Indonesia said its one-month Sertifikat Bank Indonesia note yielded 14.07% at an auction Wednesday, down from 14.35% a week earlier. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  heen been cutting interest rates to help spur economic growth to meet its gross domestic product target of 4% growth this year. \par \par \uc2  Lower yields have little effect on the spot \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market as banks aren't lending to corporate clients while nonperforming loans left behind by the crisis remain high. \par \par \uc2  -By Tom Wright, Dow Jones Newswires; 62-21 39831277; tom.wright@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1159 1848 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020020904dy94000m9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
