\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesia Rupiah Ends Dn,Tracks Yen As Local Leads Absent \b0\par\par\uc2 352 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 August 2002\par 11:37\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA -(Dow Jones)- The Indonesian rupiah ended weaker in thin trading Friday, as it tracked the Japanese yen lower against the dollar amid the lack of fresh local leads, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah rarely tracks the movement of major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the dollar, as it is usually influenced by local factors, such as political news, dollar demand from local companies and suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Such domestic drivers, however, were missing Friday. \par \par \uc2  The dollar closed at 8,885 rupiah late Friday, up from its close at IDR8,840 Thursday. \par \par \uc2  At 0910 GMT (5:10 a.m. EDT) Friday, the dollar was at Y120.08, above Y119.87 in New York late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Overall, the dollar also strengthened considerably against most \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Asia Friday, thanks to the overnight rise in U.S. stocks. \par \par \uc2  The Dow Jones Industrial Average rose 96.41 points, or 1.08%, to 9053.64 overnight Thursday, marking the first time in more than six weeks the DJIA has managed to close above 9000 points. The Nasdaq Composite index was up 1.0% at 1422 points. \par \par \uc2  Despite the dollar's gains versus the rupiah, market players remained wary of potential losses resulting from any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the rupiah, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Bank Indonesia was suspected to have sold dollars Friday to prevent the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from getting too close to the IDR9,000 psychologically crucial resistance mark. Any rise to this level is expected to accelerate the dollar's climb, making it more difficult for Bank Indonesia to curb its gains. \par \par \uc2  "I think Bank Indonesia will remain resilient in guarding the rupiah," said a dealer at a U.S. bank. \par \par \uc2  Bank Indonesia officials have said in the past that the nation's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to protect the rupiah if necessary. Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , however, usually refuses to confirm specific \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Dealers expect the dollar to trade between IDR8,850 and IDR8,890 Monday. \par \par \uc2  -By I Made Sentana, Dow Jones Newswires; 62-21 39831277; I-Made.Sentana@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1159 1848 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020020823dy8n001b2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
