\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia \highlight\uc2  Rupiah Ends Up; Rumored Ctrl Bk  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 323 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 August 2002\par 11:36\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA -(Dow Jones)- The Indonesian rupiah ended higher Wednesday amid suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a thin market, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's weaker tone against most regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  also helped push the rupiah to close higher, they said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar ended Asian trading at IDR8,830, down from IDR8,850 at Tuesday's close. \par \par \uc2  Bank Indonesia, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was rumored to have taken advantage of the thin trading to sell dollars to help the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , according to traders. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market, but rarely confirms its actions. \par \par \uc2  But strong demand from local companies that need dollars to fund debt repayment and imports lent support to the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at IDR8,830 in the afternoon, traders noted. \par \par \uc2  In a key signal of monetary policy, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  cut its overnight \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate Wednesday by 100 basis points to 12.625%, a bid to help spur economic growth. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate is the rate that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  pays commercial banks to take their deposits \par \par \uc2  Traders said the rate cuts didn't affect the rupiah spot market. \par \par \uc2  The dollar is expected to trade between IDR8,795 and IDR8,840 Thursday, they said. \par \par \uc2  Indonesia expects inflation in August to moderate from 10.5% on-year growth in July, allowing a gradual easing in monetary policy. \par \par \uc2  The government is hoping lower rates will lower the debt burden on companies and allow investment at a time when government spending is unlikely to help growth due to the Indonesia's huge $130 billion public debt. \par \par \uc2  The government is also hoping the economy will grow 5% next year, but economists have said the target looks ambitious given government spending constraints and waning exports. \par \par \uc2  Interbank rates fell Wednesday in tandem with the cut in the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Tom Wright, Dow Jones Newswires; 6221 3983 1277;\par tom.wright@dowjones.com\par -0-\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1159 1848 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020020821dy8l000k4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
