\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia \highlight\uc2  Rupiah Ends Flat; Ctrl Bk  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Suspected \b0\par\par\uc2 236 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 August 2002\par 11:32\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA -(Dow Jones)- The Indonesian rupiah finished flat against the dollar in quiet trading Tuesday, recovering from intraday lows on suspected dollar-selling by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar closed unchanged at 8,850 rupiah, having retreated from an intraday high of IDR8,880. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the dollar rallied in the morning as local companies continued to buy the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to pay off maturing offshore debts as well as to finance imports. \par \par \uc2  However, suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  around midday to prevent the dollar from nearing the psychologically-important level of IDR9,000 helped erase the dollar's gains, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Trading in the rupiah stayed subdued for the rest of the session due to the absence of fresh leads, they added. \par \par \uc2  Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials have said that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to defend the rupiah whenever is necessary. Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , however, usually refuses to confirm specific \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Dealers expect the dollar to trade within a narrow range of between IDR8,810 and IDR8,860 Wednesday as the market expects Bank Indonesia to continue to be on the lookout for any major weakening in the rupiah. \par \par \uc2  Still, dollar demand from local companies is also expected to remain strong, they said. \par \par \uc2  -By I Made Sentana, Dow Jones Newswires; 62-21 39831277; I-Made.Sentana@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1159 1848 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020020820dy8k000jr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
