\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesian Rupiah Ends Flat; Central Bk Support Suspected \b0\par\par\uc2 239 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 August 2002\par 11:30\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA -(Dow Jones)- The rupiah ended flat again Tuesday as suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  protected the local unit from the dollar's rise in Asia, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar closed at 9,080 rupiah, unchanged from its close Monday and last Friday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said that some market participants had tried to drive the dollar higher amid its advance against other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , especially the yen. \par \par \uc2  But when the dollar hit an intraday high of IDR9,110, Bank Indonesia was heard selling the dollar, putting a halt to its climb, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Still, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  didn't sell the dollar aggressively as trading volume remained relatively low, they said. \par \par \uc2  At the same time, "market participants were cautious about building long-dollar positions at current levels as concerns over the health of the U.S. economy linger," a dealer at a local bank said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said that the Jakarta foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market was unmoved by the 1.99% fall in local stocks Tuesday as the slide was mostly due to selloffs by local speculators. \par \par \uc2  This means that they don't expect a deluge of dollar buying in the coming days, which usually happens when foreign investors exit Indonesian stock market. \par \par \uc2  Dealers expect the dollar to trade between IDR9,050 and IDR9,125 Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  -By I Made Sentana,Dow Jones Newswires;62-21 39831277 I-Made.Sentana@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  115