\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia \highlight\uc2  Rupiah Ends Higher After Ctrl Bk  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 341 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 August 2002\par 11:28\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA -(Dow Jones)- The Indonesian rupiah ended higher Friday on reported \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The dollar ended at IDR9,085, lower than IDR9,140 at Thursday's close. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was in the market," a local trader said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't comment on specific actions in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. \par \par \uc2  The action involved selling about $20 million in the spot market, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Indonesia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Friday it expects interest rates to fall further this year due to benign inflation. \par \par \uc2  Bank Indonesia also thinks the rupiah will continue to climb against the dollar toward the end of the year, Deputy Governor Miranda Gultom told reporters. \par \par \uc2  "Looking forward, Bank Indonesia still expects inflation to fall. So we see an opportunity to cut interest rates further," Gultom said. \par \par \uc2  The government is easing its monetary policy to help spur economic growth. The country of 220 million people expects gross domestic product to jump about 5% this year, but this isn't enough to create new work for the thousands of new jobseekers every year. \par \par \uc2  Political stability under President Megawati Sukarnoputri during her first year in power has helped stabilize the rupiah, and reduce inflation pressures on the economy. The dollar was trading at IDR9,085 in late trade Friday, up about 12% since the start of the year. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  cut its overnight \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate - the rate offered to banks that park their rupiah-denominated funds with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  - by 50 basis points Friday to 13.625%. The rate is a signal of the country's monetary policy intentions. \par \par \uc2  The rate cuts came after the government announced Thursday that annual inflation had fallen to 10.05% in July from 11.48% in June. \par \par \uc2  -By Tom Wright, Dow Jones Newswires; 62 21 3983 1277; tom.wrightdowjones.com \par \par \uc2  (CORRECTED 1029GMT) \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA (Dow Jones)--The Indonesian rupiah ended higher Friday on reported \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  (In an item timed at 0928 GMT, the day was misstated.) \par \par \uc2  1159 1848 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020020802dy82000k9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
