\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Mixed on dollar dip, c.bank fears. \b0\par\par\uc2      By Ovais Subhani \par \uc2 725 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Juli 2002\par 12:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, July 12 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were a \par \par \uc2  mixed bag late Friday in choppy trade with players reluctant to \par \par \uc2  take aggressive positions ahead of the weekend. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The dollar's fall under 117 yen        and the absence of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the any dollar support from Japanese authorities aided the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Singapore dollar and Thai baht to recoup early\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par losses.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     But dollar-buying \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by Korea, through state-run\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par banks, kept players cautious and the won -2 and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par neighbouring Taiwan dollar depressed.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "Korean \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  does call for some caution but absence\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of the Bank of Japan is giving players some confidence that\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par they don't need to go long of dollars," said a senior dealer at\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par a Singapore bank.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Bank Indonesia was in the market to sell dollars and rescue\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the rupiah from sliding past 9,200, dealers in Jakarta said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Korean won ended onshore trade at 1,182.8 per dollar, a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par quarter percent down from Thursday's close of 1.179.5, but\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par above a 1,186.9 session low hit early in the day when state\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par banks had stepped in to buy dollars following another warning\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strength by the Finance Ministry.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers in Singapore said dollar buying by Korean state\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par banks eased as the yen rose against the dollar and exporters\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par offered dollars beyond 1,185 won.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Taiwan dollar ended the day flat at 33.284 as most\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par players stayed away from the market on wariness over \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par \f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 \par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's dollar purchases and on uncertainty on the near-term\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par direction of the closely tracked yen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Lack of trading interest sapped volumes to just $524\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par million, from $1.188 billion on Thursday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     However in Southeast Asia, dealers said players were a bit\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par more confident over the direction of the market and were quick\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to reverse their positions in favour of their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Singapore dollar bounced from a session low of 1.7534\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to retest overnight highs around 1.7460, tracking the yen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Thai baht was helped off a session low of 41.335, as\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par government comments were taken to mean an absence of\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  showed authorities were\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par comfortable with the baht's level.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Prime Minister Thaksin Shinawatra said baht strength would\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par not hurt as the economy was not solely dependent on exports. He\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par said baht strength will last for years due to a weakening\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Finance Minister Somkid Jatusripitak said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par was keeping an eye on the baht to ensure it remains\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par competitive.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Indonesian rupiah strengthened to levels beyond\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 9,100 from a two-month low of 9,170 per dollar, on dollar sales\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par by state banks which dealers in Jakarta said were acting on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par behalf of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Governor Sjahril Sabirin later warned the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par market of physical \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and said he expected the rupiah\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to strengthen "this afternoon" on improving sentiment.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  prompted local players long\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par on dollars to book profits.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Philippine peso        ended onshore trade at 50.495,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par stronger than session low 50.55, but down from Thursday's close\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of 50.335, on short covering of dollar positions and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par uncertainty over the direction of other regionals, dealers in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Manila said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par They said exporters came to the rescue of the peso, later\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in the day, selling dollars just beyond the 50.50 level.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. $0926 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     116.77       117.45         +0.58\par  Sing dlr      1.7460       1.7510         +0.29\par  Taiwan dlr    33.284       33.284         +0.00\par  Korean won   1182.70      1179.50         -0.27\par  Baht           41.06        41.15         +0.22\par  Peso           50.48        50.34         -0.29\par  Rupiah       9060.00      9050.00         -0.11\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     116.77       131.24        +12.39\par  Sing dlr      1.7460       1.8515         +6.04\par  Taiwan dlr    33.284       34.986         +5.11\par  Korean won   1182.70      1277.00         +7.97\par  Baht           41.06        44.16         +7.55\par  Peso           50.48        51.50         +2.02\par  Rupiah       9060.00     10350.00        +14.24\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020712dy7c00jlp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
