\par\par \b \uc2  Bk  \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia \highlight\uc2  Gov Confirms Ctrl Bk  \highlight22\uc2 Intervened \highlight\uc2  To Help IDR \b0\par\par\uc2 148 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Juli 2002\par 09:49\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA -(Dow Jones)- Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Sjahril Sabirin Monday confirmed the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to help the beleaguered rupiah last week. \par \par \uc2  "We have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  recently to defend the rupiah," Sjahril told reporters, confirming market talk. \par \par \uc2  According to dealers, Bank Indonesia stepped into the market last week and Monday to offset corporate demand for dollars to repay foreign debt and finance imports. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah fell to IDR8,925 a dollar early Monday from its close at IDR8,845 Friday as state companies bought dollars to pay for imports. \par \par \uc2  Sjahril said Bank Indonesia expects the rupiah to rebound to IDR8,500-IDR8,600/dollar in the near term, adding the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will stand by to help the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  -By Farida Husna, Dow Jones Newswires; 62-21 39831277; Farida.Husna@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020020708dy78000ey\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
