\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesia  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Confirms It Sold Dollars Friday \b0\par\par\uc2 232 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Juni 2002\par 04:27\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA -(Dow Jones)- \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  confirmed it had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Friday, selling dollars to help support the rupiah, Deputy Governor Anwar Nasution told reporters Monday. \par \par \uc2  "We \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market Friday to prevent market volatility," Nasution said. "The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was not significant in size." \par \par \uc2  The dollar closed Friday at 8,925 rupiah, down from IDR9,060 at Thursday's close, and lower than an IDR9,040 intraday high amid rumors of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Nasution didn't say, however, exactly how many dollars the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has said it's happy with the dollar in a IDR8,500 to IDR9,000 range as this is good for exporters. \par \par \uc2  Early Monday, the dollar is trading a touch lower than Friday's close at IDR8,890, again on talk that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is selling the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  through state banks. Nasution didn't comment on this. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was on a bullish path last week due to concerns over delays in Indonesia's asset sales program, which means the country's debt remains at huge levels. \par \par \uc2  Jakarta is keen to keep the dollar below IDR9,000 to ease inflation and allow interest rates to drop further, helping the ailing economy. \par \par \uc2  -By Linda Silaen, Dow Jones Newswires; 6221 3983 1277; linda.silaen@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020020610dy6a0003f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
