\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia \highlight\uc2  Rupiah Ends Up On Reported Ctrl Bk  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 345 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Juni 2002\par 11:25\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA -(Dow Jones)- The rupiah ended higher Friday amid rumor of minor \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar closed at IDR8,925, down from IDR9,060 at Thursday's close, after trading in a range between IDR8,915 and IDR9,040. \par \par \uc2  Indonesia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was rumored to have sold $10 million to help support the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The bank never comments on its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  actions, but Deputy Governor Miranda Gultom said earlier this week it was happy with a IDR8,500 to IDR9,000 range for the dollar as this was good for exporters. \par \par \uc2  The dollar's decline against other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  also helped set the tone for the rupiah. \par \par \uc2  Friday's dollar decline ended a huge rise in the past two days after a slew of disappointing delays in Indonesia's efforts to sell state-owned assets to reduce huge public debt. The sales are also seen as crucial to get foreign direct investment coming back to the country. \par \par \uc2  Jakarta again canceled a meeting Friday to decide what to do with Bank Niaga after canceling an auction of a 51% stake in the bank last week due to low bids. Further delays could hurt the rupiah, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Such bad news punctured weeks of exuberance toward the rupiah, which was trading at nine month highs against the dollar at IDR8,840 earlier this week. \par \par \uc2  But for now, the dollar's rise seems to be over, and the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to settle into a range between IDR8,850 and IDR8,950 next week. \par \par \uc2  Pessimism toward the slow pace of asset sales is tempered by Indonesia's continued political stability under President Megawati Sukarnoputri and the support of supranational lenders such as the International Monetary Fund toward Indonesia. \par \par \uc2  United Overseas Bank said in a research note Friday it expects the U.S. unit to fall back toward IDR8,600 in the coming weeks. \par \par \uc2  -By Tom Wright, Dow Jones Newswires; 6221 3983 1277; tom.wright@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1159 1848 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020020607dy67000k1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
