\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Down on yen losses, c.bank fears. \b0\par\par\uc2      By Ovais Subhani \par \uc2 868 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Juni 2002\par 11:42\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, June 5 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  backtracked \par \par \uc2  on some of their recent gains on Wednesday following the yen \par \par \uc2   which stayed depressed after last night's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  by the Bank of Japan in favour of the dollar. \par \par \uc2      That was BOJ's fourth \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in recent days although \par \par \uc2  it failed to convince the market that it would continue to \par \par \uc2  stand in the way of any yen appreciation from here, but did \par \par \uc2  manage to keep a lid on short dollar positions. \par \par \uc2      The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  also made players in regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  wary of similar actions by their central banks. \par \par \uc2      Taking advantage of that wariness, officials in Seoul \par \par \uc2  stepped up their verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to pull the Korean won \par \par \uc2  -2 off its recent multi-month highs against the dollar. \par \par \uc2      Japan is both a major trading market and competitor for \par \par \uc2  most other Asian countries, so regional policy makers tend to \par \par \uc2  use dollar/yen as a measure of their competitiveness. \par \par \uc2      But in the case of Korea they also keep an eye on the \par \par \uc2  yen/won cross , which has appreciated from levels \par \par \uc2  above 10 won in mid-April to around 9.7 won in recent sessions. \par \par \uc2      WON TALKED DOWN \par \par \uc2      Both the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and officials of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of\b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  were in the market to talk the won down, pulling it to \par \par \uc2  a session low of 1,225 per dollar, against a five-and-a-half \par \par \uc2  month high of 1,219.9 hit on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2      The won ended onshore trade at 1,224.3, versus Tuesday's \par \par \uc2  close of 1,220.10. \par \par \uc2      Dealers in Singapore said the market gave little response \par \par \uc2  to a widely expected \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  decision to leave the key \par \par \uc2  overnight call rate target unchanged at 4.25 percent. \par \par \uc2      The market also failed to react to \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief Park \par \par \uc2  Seung's statement that he saw economy growing by six to seven \par \par \uc2  percent, against last year's three percent and an earlier \par \par \uc2  forecast of 5.7 percent. \par \par \uc2  But what the market heard loud and clear was his statement \par \par \uc2  that the won's rise, near six percent so far this year, would \par \par \uc2  hurt export competitiveness and monetary authorities were ready \par \par \uc2  to take action if necessary. \par \par \uc2  Later Kim Yong-duk, responsible for the Finance Ministry's \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said it was about time to take \par \par \uc2  action to tame the won's steep rise. \par \par \uc2  BI DENIES \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  comments were also the main focus in \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  where the rupiah slid to a near two-week low of 8,975, \par \par \uc2  as players bailed out of short dollar positions, uncertain \par \par \uc2  about the the bank's position on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and depressed by \par \par \uc2  recent delays in the sale of state assets. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  came out to deny rumours it was buying \par \par \uc2  dollars to cap the rupiah's recent gains and said 8,500-8,600 \par \par \uc2  was an appropriate range for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  On Tuesday, the rupiah touched a high of 8,440, its highest \par \par \uc2  since August 21, before the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  warned the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  market not to overreact on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strength which could lead \par \par \uc2  to excessive swings and affect economic recovery. \par \par \uc2  The momentum of the rupiah's fall eased a bit, pushing the \par \par \uc2  rupiah back to 8,900, and was further helped by the benchmark \par \par \uc2  one-month SBI interest rate that fell in the weekly auction to \par \par \uc2  15.17 percent from 15.51 percent in the previous auction. \par \par \uc2  PESO, SGD & BAHT \par \par \uc2  Inflation data in Philippines had little impact on the peso \par \par \uc2  , which eased to 50.80 from Tuesday's close of 50.43, \par \par \uc2  mainly on political worries after the defection of Senator John \par \par \uc2  Osmena to the opposition, tilting the balance in the Senate \par \par \uc2  against President Gloria Macapagal Arroyo. \par \par \uc2      Philippines inflation in May rose by an expected 3.6 \par \par \uc2  percent and was unchanged from April. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Singapore dollar        eased to a one-week low of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1.7955 per dollar, from late Tuesday's 1.7825, weighed down by\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the yen's losses against the dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Thai baht        also tracked the regional mood and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par slipped to bump against one-week lows at 42.535 before bouncing\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par back to 42.49, still down from late Tuesday's 42.29.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers said slowing equity and export-related inflows also\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par weighed on the baht.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S.       $0922 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     124.51       123.38         -0.91\par  Sing dlr      1.7943       1.7825         -0.66\par  Taiwan dlr    34.097       34.093         -0.01\par  Korean won   1205.10      1220.10         +1.24\par  Baht           42.49        42.29         -0.47\par  Peso           50.83        50.43         -0.79\par  Rupiah       8890.00      8650.00         -2.70\par  Ringgit       3.7997       3.7995         -0.01\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     124.51       131.24         +5.41\par  Sing dlr      1.7943       1.8515         +3.19\par  Taiwan dlr    34.097       34.986         +2.61\par  Korean won   1205.10      1277.00         +5.97\par  Baht           42.49        44.16         +3.93\par  Peso           50.83        51.50         +1.32\par  Rupiah       8890.00     10350.00        +16.42\par  Ringgit       3.7997       3.7995         -0.01.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020605dy6500iu6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
