\par\par \b \uc2  Bank  \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia \highlight\uc2  denies dollar buying  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 161 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Juni 2002\par 11:27\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, June 5 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday denied market talk it was buying dollars saying there was more room for the rupiah to continue its recent surge. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah - the best performing regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  this year - lost some of its gains after the bank said on Tuesday the market should not over react to the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's appreciation. \par \par \uc2  Some dealers took those remarks as a signal that the bank would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem the rupiah's sharp rise. \par \par \uc2  "It is impossible (for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) to buy dollars because there is still room for the rupiah to strengthen," \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  deputy governor Miranda Goeltom told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  Goeltom said a rupiah level of around 8,500-8,600 to the dollar was "appropriate". \par \par \uc2  By 0925 GMT on Wednesday, the rupiah was quoted at 8,890/8,940 per dollar after touching its highest level since August 21 of 8,440 the previous day. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020605dy6500idl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
