\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesia Rupiah Ends Dn As Importers, Comml Bks Buy Dlrs \b0\par\par\uc2 265 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Februar 2002\par 10:22\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA -(Dow Jones)- The Indonesian rupiah closed lower Thursday as commercial banks covered their short-dollar positions amid fresh bids for the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by local importers, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar closed at 10,215 rupiah, up from its close at IDR10,180 Wednesday. The dollar, however, was off its intraday high of IDR10,260 on suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has said it would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to defend the rupiah if necessary. It doesn't comment on specific instances of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , however. \par \par \uc2  "Fresh bids for dollars from local importers triggered interbank players to square their dollar-short positions," said a dealer with a foreign bank. \par \par \uc2  Dealers expect banks to drive the dollar lower to IDR10,180 when the market reopens Friday before local companies step in to buy the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on dips. \par \par \uc2  Besides buying dollars to pay for imports, local companies need dollars to pay maturing offshore debts. \par \par \uc2  Dealers expect the dollar to trade between IDR10,180 and IDR10,250 Friday. \par \par \uc2  In the money market, the overnight rupiah lending rate slipped to 15.75% from 16% earlier in the day on improved liquidity. But the rate was still higher than its usual level of between 15.25% and 15.50%, as the Indonesian Bank Restructuring Agency was suspected to have withdrawn some of the funds it had placed with banks and transferred them to the state coffers. \par \par \uc2  -By I Made Sentana, Dow Jones Newswires; 62-21 39831277; I-Made.Sentana@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1159 1848 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020020214dy2e000jm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
