\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Directionless, market in holiday mood. \b0\par\par\uc2 666 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Februar 2002\par 10:38\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, Feb 11 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were a mixed \par \par \uc2  bag in thin trade late on Monday as players did last-minute \par \par \uc2  position squaring ahead of Lunar New Year holidays. \par \par \uc2      Trading was thinned by local holiday in Japan and Lunar New \par \par \uc2  Year holidays in Korea and Taiwan. Most Asian financial markets \par \par \uc2  will be closed on Tuesday and Wednesday. \par \par \uc2      Markets showed no response to Singapore's official upgrade \par \par \uc2  of its growth forecast while the absence of corporate demand \par \par \uc2  for dollars pushed the Thai baht and the Indonesian rupiah \par \par \uc2  higher. \par \par \uc2  "The market seemed to be paying more attention to what they \par \par \uc2  are going to eat at New Year banquets than to the global or \par \par \uc2  regional outlook today," said a dealer at an Asian bank. \par \par \uc2  The G7 meeting over the weekend hardly affected the market \par \par \uc2  as the meeting passed without any strong comments on \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The yen bounced off its early lows as players covered short \par \par \uc2  positions in anticipation of fund repatriation by Japanese \par \par \uc2  firms and on expectations of supportive comments ahead of \par \par \uc2  President George W. Bush's visit to Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar lingered within a narrow 1.8325-1.8340 \par \par \uc2  range in choppy trade. \par \par \uc2  Most players reluctant to take fresh positions ahead of the \par \par \uc2  Tuesday-Wednesday holidays, even as Prime Minister Goh Chok \par \par \uc2  Tong said in a Lunar New Year message the government had \par \par \uc2  revised growth expectations for the year to 1.0 to 3.0 percent, \par \par \uc2  up from minus 2.0 to plus 2.0 percent. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the upward revision was behind the curve \par \par \uc2  because most analysts had been raising their forecasts since \par \par \uc2  the end of 2001, when exports in most Asian showed signs of \par \par \uc2  bottoming out. \par \par \uc2  THAI BAHT \par \par \uc2  The baht was in a doldrum as players wound up their trading \par \par \uc2  ahead of the holiday. Although Thai financial markets are open \par \par \uc2  during Lunar New Year, a number of Chinese-Thai companies will \par \par \uc2  be closed. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the baht had been underpinned lately by dollar \par \par \uc2  offers from offshore names in Singapore and Hong Kong, and \par \par \uc2  capital inflows from a Japanese auto maker. \par \par \uc2  Baht funding costs in the offshore market were soft, with \par \par \uc2  the one-month forward rate being quoted at 5/10 satang to the \par \par \uc2  dollar. \par \par \uc2  PHILIPPINE PESO \par \par \uc2  The peso ended lower at 51.315 to the dollar against 51.220 \par \par \uc2  on Friday after corporates stocked up for debt repayment. \par \par \uc2  Turnover picked up to $100.75 million from around $86 million \par \par \uc2  in the previous session. \par \par \uc2  However, analysts expect the peso to strengthen in the \par \par \uc2  medium term on the back of inflows from equity investment and \par \par \uc2  asset sales. \par \par \uc2  In the money market, the country's key Treasury bill rate \par \par \uc2  fell below the benchmark overnight borrowing rate at Monday's \par \par \uc2  government auction to a fresh 15-year low of 7.278 percent, and \par \par \uc2  the government said it hoped the 91-day T-bill would fall \par \par \uc2  further. \par \par \uc2  INDONESIAN RUPIAH \par \par \uc2  The rupiah edged higher as local corporates stayed out of \par \par \uc2  the market, allowing interbank players to further trim their \par \par \uc2  long dollar positions. \par \par \uc2  The long dollar liquidation was kicked off after aggressive \par \par \uc2  dollar purchases by state banks sparked talk of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  last week. \par \par \uc2      Financial markets in \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be closed on Tuesday \par \par \uc2  and will reopen on Wednesday. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0746 GMT \par \par \uc2   Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     134.33       133.66         -0.50\par  Sing dlr      1.8323       1.8309         -0.08\par  Baht           43.88        43.88         +0.00\par  Peso           51.30        51.22         -0.16\par  Rupiah      10185.00     10251.00         +0.65\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     134.33       131.24         -2.30\par  Sing dlr      1.8323       1.8515         +1.05\par  Baht           43.88        44.16         +0.64\par  Peso           51.30        51.50         +0.39\par  Rupiah      10185.00     10350.00         +1.62\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020211dy2b00j50\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
