\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Mixed in Asia as dollar/yen idles. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,070 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Januar 2002\par 03:16\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, Jan 10 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  parted ways \par \par \uc2  early on Thursday, with most edging lower or steady, as the \par \par \uc2  dollar dithered just under the 133 level against the yen. \par \par \uc2      The markets remained fixated on the wobbly yen's progress, \par \par \uc2  and any sharp movement in the dollar/yen could trigger a \par \par \uc2  reaction in the regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2      But, in keeping with their recent trend, any reaction was \par \par \uc2  likely to be muted. \par \par \uc2      Analysts have attributed the more modest losses of the \par \par \uc2  regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  compared to the yen's to a number of \par \par \uc2  factors including recent capital inflows into the region and \par \par \uc2  already substantial falls in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  However, they have reminded the market it would be \par \par \uc2  foolhardy to believe the Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have cut their apron \par \par \uc2  strings with the yen. \par \par \uc2  "While Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  notable the KRW, TWD and SGD have \par \par \uc2  outperformed the JPY since September 11, they have done so \par \par \uc2  because markets are pricing in a firm rebound in the U.S.," \par \par \uc2  said Mansoor Mohi-uddin, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at UBS Warburg in \par \par \uc2  Singapore, said in a note. \par \par \uc2  "If this fails to materialise then Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are \par \par \uc2  likely to come under renewed pressure against the JPY as well \par \par \uc2  as the USD." \par \par \uc2  On the local news front, both the Bank of Korea and the \par \par \uc2  Philippine \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be holding monetary policy \par \par \uc2  meetings later in the day. \par \par \uc2  KOREAN WON -2 \par \par \uc2  The won edged lower in line with the yen, but gains on the \par \par \uc2  local stock market were expected to boost its fortunes. \par \par \uc2      However, players were wary that the authorities, unhappy \par \par \uc2  with the won's surge against the yen, may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2      Deputy Finance Minister Kim Yong-Duk told Reuters on \par \par \uc2  Wednesday that a weaker won should accompany any more falls in \par \par \uc2  the yen for Korea to maintain export competitiveness. \par \par \uc2      He also said the attempts by Japanese officials to talk \par \par \uc2  down the yen were "undesirable", and warned it could provoke \par \par \uc2  concerns from Japan's neighbours in Asia. \par \par \uc2      The Bank of Korea is expected to keep its key overnight \par \par \uc2  call rate steady at four percent at its monthly monetary policy \par \par \uc2  meeting later in the day. In a recent Reuters poll, economists \par \par \uc2  said expectations of a better economy were likely to encourage \par \par \uc2  the bank to sit pat on rates. \par \par \uc2  THAI BAHT \par \par \uc2  The baht was mostly steady in early trade in a dearth of \par \par \uc2  fresh leads, with most market participants focused on the \par \par \uc2  direction of the dollar/yen and real commercial demand. \par \par \uc2  In the medium term, dealers expected the baht to be \par \par \uc2  well-supported by expectations of capital inflows linked to \par \par \uc2  privatisation, with the state-owned Telephone Organisation of \par \par \uc2  Thailand (TOT) launching its IPO in March. \par \par \uc2  In the offshore market, baht funding costs were hardly \par \par \uc2  changed, with the tom/next rate at 0/5 satang per dollar and \par \par \uc2  the one-month rate at 7/11 satang per dollar. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Sing dollar was marginally weaker, but off its morning \par \par \uc2  low of 1.8520 after some U.S. and European names cashed in on \par \par \uc2  the U.S. dollar gains. \par \par \uc2  But dollar bargain hunting at around 1.8460 would mean that \par \par \uc2  the Sing dollar will trade in a narrow range, with players \par \par \uc2  focused mostly on the dollar/yen direction, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the Sing dollar's downside should be limited \par \par \uc2  in the longer term after the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore \par \par \uc2  restored a narrow trading band earlier this month. \par \par \uc2  "This implies that the MAS will be less tolerant of Sing \par \par \uc2  dollar weakness against the USD going forward," said Mohi-uddin \par \par \uc2  at UBS Warburg. \par \par \uc2  PHILIPPINE PESO (PHP=) \par \par \uc2  The peso opened at 51.80, edging lower than the previous \par \par \uc2  day's close of 51.56, but dealers in Manila said the \par \par \uc2  government's launch of 15-year global bonds would give a slight \par \par \uc2  boost to the peso. \par \par \uc2  Co-lead manager of the bond issue Morgan Stanley said on \par \par \uc2  Wednesday the Philippines sold $750 million of 15-year global \par \par \uc2  bonds. Dealers said the market was hoping the sale of those \par \par \uc2  bonds might bring fresh dollar inflows into the market should \par \par \uc2  the government choose to inject some of that liquidity from the \par \par \uc2  bond launch into the market. \par \par \uc2      They were mixed on whether the Philippine \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  would cut rates later in the day. \par \par \uc2      Dealers in Manila and Singapore expected the peso to trade \par \par \uc2  at an intraday high of 51.50 to the dollar because corporates \par \par \uc2  were buying dollars at that level. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     TAIWAN DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Taiwan dollar was barely changed from Wednesday's close\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of 35.05 as the market waited for fresh cues from the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar/yen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Still, the market was reluctant to take any large positions\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par because volatility was expected to be held in check by the\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . Taiwan's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  boasts some $122 billion in\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves, and market players say it is\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par regularly in the market to smooth away volatility.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was also likely to receive a boost from\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par continued foreign fund flows into the local stock market.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par      INDONESIAN RUPIAH\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The rupiah drifted around a narrow range of 10,400-10,500\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par with the market still suffering from the lack of fresh leads.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     While local corporate dollar demand has re-emerged in the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par market, dealers in Jakarta said players were reluctant to take\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par huge positions because of fears of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     On the macro front, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's Chief Economics Minister\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dorodjatun Kuntjoro-Jakti told Reuters the economy should grow\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par by four percent this year compared with 3.5 percent last year.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. $0156 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     132.80       132.66         -0.11\par  Sing dlr      1.8470       1.8459         -0.06\par  Taiwan dlr    35.044       35.050         +0.02\par  Korean won   1301.90      1311.90         +0.77\par  Baht           44.07        44.06         -0.02\par  Peso           51.45        51.56         +0.21\par  Rupiah      10400.00     10410.00         +0.10\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     132.80       131.24         -1.17\par  Sing dlr      1.8470       1.8515         +0.24\par  Taiwan dlr    35.044       34.986         -0.17\par  Korean won   1301.90      1313.00         +0.85\par  Baht           44.07        44.16         +0.20\par  Peso           51.45        51.50         +0.10\par  Rupiah      10400.00     10350.00         -0.48\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020110dy1a004h7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
