\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Trapped under yen's shadow. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,060 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Januar 2002\par 04:08\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, Jan 4 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  held onto \par \par \uc2  their recent ranges early on Friday, but the yen's shaky shadow \par \par \uc2  was stretching over regional markets. \par \par \uc2      With little fresh local news to trade on, players have been \par \par \uc2  focused on the yen, which continued to battle the dollar \par \par \uc2  despite the euro's slight retreat. \par \par \uc2      Still, there were local factors that managed to dull the \par \par \uc2  yen's influence. Foreign equity inflows in South Korea and \par \par \uc2  Taiwan's stock markets cushioned some of the negative vibes \par \par \uc2  from the yen, with fear of Taiwan's ever-vigilant \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  also doing an effective job of protecting the Taiwan dollar. \par \par \uc2  A bit of jawboning from Thai authorities also aided the \par \par \uc2  baht. And players in Singapore were taking seriously the \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore's decision to narrow the \par \par \uc2  trading band for the trade-weighted Singapore dollar as a \par \par \uc2  reflection of improving confidence in the economy. \par \par \uc2  There was some local data expected to trickle in later in \par \par \uc2  the day, including Philippine export numbers for November and \par \par \uc2  December inflation. \par \par \uc2  But both the major and regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets were \par \par \uc2  paying the most attention on U.S. employment report for \par \par \uc2  December due later in the day. \par \par \uc2  KOREAN WON -2 \par \par \uc2  The won is firmer against the U.S. dollar, boosted by gains \par \par \uc2  in the stock market, a rebound in the yen and talk of exporter \par \par \uc2  dollar offers. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  opened a touch lower at 1,313.0 against \par \par \uc2  Thursday's close of 1,312.7 before climbing to its morning high \par \par \uc2  of 1,308.5. \par \par \uc2  Korean shares jumped three percent after the first \par \par \uc2  eight minutes of trading, fuelling hopes for foreign capital \par \par \uc2  inflows. \par \par \uc2  Foreign investors bought a net 211 billion won worth of \par \par \uc2  shares on Korean bourses on Thursday, almost double their net \par \par \uc2  buying the previous day. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said seasonal demand, the yen's direction and local \par \par \uc2  stocks would continue to be major driver in the near-term. \par \par \uc2  Charts show 1,300 is a strong resistance for the won for now. \par \par \uc2  TAIWAN DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar opened firmer at 35.003 to the dollar in \par \par \uc2  the onshore market compared with 35.030 at Thursday's close. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was supported by a steady yen and hopes for \par \par \uc2  more capital inflows after the local stocks racked up gains at \par \par \uc2  the open because U.S. gains boosted local semiconductor shares. \par \par \uc2      Foreign investors were net buyers of T$5.31 billion (US$152 \par \par \uc2  million) in Taiwan stocks on Thursday. \par \par \uc2      The Finance Ministry will release December trade data on \par \par \uc2  Monday. \par \par \uc2      The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data show Taiwan's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  reserves rose to a record US$122.211 billion in December, \par \par \uc2  making the sixth straight monthly rise. \par \par \uc2      Although the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  did not give the reason for the \par \par \uc2  rise, dealers said it had been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  actively in the \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in December to curb gains in the Taiwan \par \par \uc2  dollar and support Taiwan's export competitiveness. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar held steady within a tight \par \par \uc2  1.8470-1.8475 range, helped by a steadier yen. \par \par \uc2  But dealers said expected near-term weakness of the yen and \par \par \uc2  talk of dollar bids by local players lined up at around 1.8440 \par \par \uc2  would keep Sing dollar's upside limited. \par \par \uc2  Dollar offers were expected at around 1.8500 with most \par \par \uc2  players reluctant to test lower levels after the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2  Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore narrowed its preferred trading band for \par \par \uc2  the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  PHILIPPINE PESO \par \par \uc2  The peso edged slightly higher as interbank players \par \par \uc2  continued to trim their long dollar positions on a steadier \par \par \uc2  yen. \par \par \uc2  However, dealers in Manila said the peso's upside would be \par \par \uc2  limited on an expected rise in demand for dollars by local \par \par \uc2  corporates next week. \par \par \uc2  The market will watch out for the inflation data for \par \par \uc2  December, due to be released later in the day, for clues on the \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's next move on key interest rates. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday left key overnight rates \par \par \uc2  unchanged with borrowing at 7.75 percent and lending at 10 \par \par \uc2  percent. The rates were last lowered by 25 basis points on \par \par \uc2  December 13. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor said there was room for another \par \par \uc2  25-50 basis point cut in key rates later this month depending \par \par \uc2  on factors like inflation and economic recovery. \par \par \uc2  THAI BAHT \par \par \uc2  The baht was stalling just below the 44 level as players \par \par \uc2  pondered the dollar/yen's next move. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in Singapore said comments by the Thai finance \par \par \uc2  minister and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor that 44 to the dollar was an \par \par \uc2  appropriate level for the baht had a limited impact on the \par \par \uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  Bank of Thailand governor Pridiyathorn Devakula said on \par \par \uc2  Thursday the bank would monitor the exchange rate more closely \par \par \uc2  this year because exports are expected to run into more \par \par \uc2  trouble. \par \par \uc2  Daily charts showed the dollar/baht retracing some of its \par \par \uc2  move up in late December, with 43.95 expected to provide some \par \par \uc2  support because it represents the 50 percent retracement of its \par \par \uc2  December 13-28 rise. \par \par \uc2  INDONESIAN RUPIAH \par \par \uc2  The rupiah managed to stay afloat above the 10,400 mark on \par \par \uc2  wariness over possible \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  With few positive local factors to drive it higher, the \par \par \uc2  rupiah was content to stagnate around these levels as players \par \par \uc2  acted cautiously in case of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  A newspaper reported the economy grew by 3.5 percent in \par \par \uc2  2001 according to preliminary figures, slightly beating \par \par \uc2  expectations of 3.01 percent growth. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0121 GMT \par \par \uc2   Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     131.58       131.71         +0.10\par  Sing dlr      1.8455       1.8475         +0.11\par  Taiwan dlr    34.995       35.030         +0.10\par  Korean won   1310.00      1312.50         +0.19\par  Baht           43.98        44.06         +0.19\par  Peso           51.57        51.61         +0.08\par  Rupiah      10335.00     10380.00         +0.44\par  Ringgit       3.7998       3.7995         -0.01\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     131.58       131.24         -0.26\par  Sing dlr      1.8455       1.8515         +0.33\par  Taiwan dlr    34.995       34.986         -0.03\par  Korean won   1310.00      1313.00         +0.23\par  Baht           43.98        44.16         +0.42\par  Peso           51.57        51.50         -0.14\par  Rupiah      10335.00     10350.00         +0.15\par  Ringgit       3.7998       3.7995         -0.01.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020104dy1400464\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
