\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesia Rupiah Ends Lower On Dollar Debt Repayments \b0\par\par\uc2 328 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Januar 2002\par 10:34\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA -(Dow Jones)- The Indonesian rupiah ended weaker Thursday as banks bought dollars on behalf of corporate clients that need to repay debt. \par \par \uc2  Negative sentiment was further compounded by demonstrations earlier this week against plans to raise utility costs this year to ease the budget deficit. \par \par \uc2  The government needs to get its deficit - estimated at 3.7% of gross domestic product last year - under control to restore confidence in the economy and the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Failure to do so will leave Indonesia even more dependent on foreign loans to fill the gap. \par \par \uc2  The dollar ended at IDR10,390-IDR10,410, higher than IDR10,380 at Wednesday's close. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traded up to an intraday high at IDR10,430, at this level the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was rumored to have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  by selling dollars. The bank has a policy of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to help the rupiah, but never confirms its actions. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to defend IDR10,450 Friday, making this a key resistance level for the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Although the bank's dollar sales can bring the U.S. unit lower in thin trade, the trend is likely to remain dollar bullish in the near term, traders said. Many \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  players remain on holiday this week after the New Year break. \par \par \uc2  But next week, the dollar may continue to rise amid further demand from local companies that need to repay foreign debt. \par \par \uc2  The government, too, is burdened with huge foreign public debt totaling around $70 billion. Jakarta is likely to have to ask foreign government creditors at a meeting next month to reschedule its debt coming due this year. \par \par \uc2  Without faster sales of assets from the broken banking system - which crashed in 1997 bringing the economy to its knees - the government deficit will remain high, and the rupiah under pressure. \par \par \uc2  -By Tom Wright, Dow Jones Newswires; 6221 3983 1277; tom.wright@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1159 1848 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020020103dy13000fm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
