\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia \highlight\uc2  Rupiah Ends Up;Ctrl Bank  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Suspected \b0\par\par\uc2 313 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Januar 2002\par 10:55\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA -(Dow Jones)- The Indonesian rupiah ended slightly higher on its first trading for the year Wednesday thanks to suspected Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar closed at 10,380 rupiah, down from its close Friday at IDR10,450. Indonesian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets were closed Monday and Tuesday for New Year's holidays. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. unit had risen to an intraday high of IDR10,550 earlier in the day as some participants bought the dollar on expectations of corporate demand. \par \par \uc2  However, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was suspected to have entered the market, which triggered the unwinding of the dollar-long positions. Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  has a policy of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent volatility, but it doesn't comment on individual actions. \par \par \uc2  "Talk that Bank Indonesia was in the market quickly triggered dollar-long liquidation as basically the dollar was already overbought," a dealer with a local bank said. \par \par \uc2  Local companies, which in most recent sessions have been buying dollars for debt servicing, were absent from the market. \par \par \uc2  Fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  protected the rupiah from news that the country's trade surplus in November narrowed to $1.8 billion from $2.46 billion in October. \par \par \uc2  Continued weak data for both exports and imports indicate that economic growth may remain soft this year, and the weaker surplus points to a possible future deterioration in reserves, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers expect the dollar to trade between IDR10,350 and IDR10,450 Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Separately, the weighted average rate of Bank Indonesia's one-month Sertifikat Bank Indonesia notes edged down to 17.50% in a weekly auction from 17.62% last week. \par \par \uc2  The decline, however, was too little to indicate a softening bias on the part of Bank Indonesia, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  -By I Made Sentana, Dow Jones Newswires; 62-21 39831277; I-Made.Sentana@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1159 1848 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020020102dy12000h1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
