\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesia Rupiah Ends Down;Local Cos Buy Dlr On Last Day \b0\par\par\uc2 245 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Dezember 2001\par 10:30\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2001, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA -(Dow Jones)- The Indonesian rupiah gave up earlier gains to close slightly lower in thin trade Friday as local companies bought the dollar on dips to pay maturing foreign debts, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  After falling to an intraday low of 10,300 rupiah, the dollar closed at IDR10,450, up from its close Thursday at IDR10,410. \par \par \uc2  This means the rupiah depreciated 7.4% this year compared with its close at IDR9,675 to the dollar last year. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. unit fell to its intraday low on suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. The nation's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has said that it would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to help the local unit, but it won't comment on individual actions. \par \par \uc2  Still, the dollar's slide only proved an invitation for local companies to buy the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  during the year's last trading day. \par \par \uc2  Trading will be closed Monday as Bank Indonesia won't provide clearing services ahead of the New Year public holiday. The local foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market will reopen Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers expect the dollar to start the new year with bullish note as local companies will still have to pay maturing offshore debts next year. \par \par \uc2  Moreover, a lack of progress on the domestic economy will continue to deter foreign investment in Indonesia, dealers added. \par \par \uc2  -By I Made Sentana,Dow Jones Newswires;62-21 39831277 I-Made.Sentana@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  115